---
export const prerender = true;
import AppLayout from '../layouts/AppLayout.astro';
const updated = 'June 30, 2026';
---

<AppLayout
  title="Terms of Service - Pixelatmos"
  description="The terms that govern your use of Pixelatmos's creative tools and wallpaper gallery."
>
  <div class="legal-container">
    <div class="content-wrapper">
      <h1 class="glitch-title">Terms of Service</h1>

      <div class="text-content">
        <p class="updated">Last updated: {updated}</p>

        <h2 class="first-heading">1. Agreement</h2>
        <p>
          These Terms of Service ("Terms") govern your access to and use of Pixelatmos
          (the "Site"), including its browser-based creative tools (ASCII Lab, Visual
          Protocol, 3D Lab) and its curated wallpaper gallery. By accessing or using the
          Site you agree to these Terms. If you do not agree, please do not use the Site.
        </p>

        <h2>2. The Service</h2>
        <p>
          Pixelatmos provides free, browser-based creative tools and a gallery of
          original tech-culture wallpapers. The creative tools run entirely in your
          browser (client-side): the assets you paste, type, or upload are processed
          locally on your device and are not uploaded to or stored on our servers unless
          a specific feature explicitly states otherwise.
        </p>

        <h2>3. Acceptable Use</h2>
        <p>You agree not to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>use the Site for any unlawful purpose or in violation of any applicable law;</li>
          <li>attempt to disrupt, overload, reverse-engineer, or gain unauthorized access to the Site or its infrastructure;</li>
          <li>upload content you do not have the right to use, or content that infringes the rights of others;</li>
          <li>use automated systems to scrape or redistribute Site content at scale.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>4. Intellectual Property &amp; Licensing</h2>
        <p>
          The wallpapers, branding, interface, and original code of Pixelatmos are the
          property of Pixelatmos and its creator, except where third-party components
          are used under their own licenses. Wallpaper usage rights are described on our
          <a href="/license">License</a> page. The 3D Lab tool is built on the open-source
          <a href="https://github.com/renatoworks/3dsvg" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">3dsvg</a>
          engine (MIT © Renato Costa); see the <a href="/license">License</a> page for details.
        </p>

        <h2>5. Your Content</h2>
        <p>
          You retain all rights to any file (e.g. an SVG) you provide to the creative
          tools. Because processing happens in your browser, you are solely responsible
          for the content you supply and for ensuring you have the rights to use it. Any
          output you generate with the tools is yours to use, subject to any third-party
          rights in the source material you supplied.
        </p>

        <h2>6. Advertising</h2>
        <p>
          The Site may display advertising provided by third parties, including Google
          AdSense. Advertisers and ad networks may use cookies and similar technologies to
          serve ads based on your prior visits. Our handling of advertising cookies is
          described in our <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Disclaimers</h2>
        <p>
          The Site and its tools are provided "as is" and "as available", without
          warranties of any kind, whether express or implied, including fitness for a
          particular purpose. We do not warrant that the Site will be uninterrupted,
          error-free, or secure.
        </p>

        <h2>8. Limitation of Liability</h2>
        <p>
          To the maximum extent permitted by law, Pixelatmos and its creator shall not
          be liable for any indirect, incidental, or consequential damages arising from
          your use of, or inability to use, the Site or its tools.
        </p>

        <h2>9. Changes to These Terms</h2>
        <p>
          We may update these Terms from time to time. Material changes will be reflected
          by updating the "Last updated" date above. Continued use of the Site after
          changes take effect constitutes acceptance of the revised Terms.
        </p>

        <h2>10. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about these Terms? Reach out through our
          <a href="/contact/">Contact</a> page.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</AppLayout>

<style>
  .legal-container {
    min-height: 80vh;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 60px 20px;
    background: #0a0a0f;
    color: #f0f0f0;
  }
  .content-wrapper {
    max-width: 800px;
    width: 100%;
  }
  .glitch-title {
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4rem);
    font-weight: 900;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    color: #f0f0f0;
    text-shadow: 2px 2px 0px #b026ff, -2px -2px 0px #00fff9;
  }
  .text-content {
    background: #121218;
    border: 1px solid #333;
    padding: 40px;
    border-radius: 8px;
    box-shadow: 0 10px 30px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5);
  }
  h2 {
    color: #00fff9;
    font-size: 1.6rem;
    margin-top: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    font-weight: 800;
  }
  .first-heading {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  p {
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: #a0a0a0;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
  }
  .updated {
    color: #666;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    font-family: monospace;
  }
  a {
    color: #00fff9;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
  a:hover {
    color: #b026ff;
  }
  ul {
    list-style-type: disc;
    padding-left: 20px;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    color: #a0a0a0;
  }
  li {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
</style>
